# The paths whose change ships to users: a commit on main that touches one of them
# (and carries no [skip release]) cuts a launcher release. One entry per line: a
# file, or dir/** for everything under dir. # starts a comment.
#
# Read by hack/release_cas.sh (its git log path filter for push runs and
# mode=changed dispatches). .github/workflows/auto-release.yml repeats the list as
# its literal push paths: (GitHub reads no file there); tests/ci_wiring_test.sh
# checks the two are equal, and that this list covers every file
# packaging/nfpm/nfpm.yaml and Formula/k3d-gpu.rb install (README.md and
# LICENSE.md excepted: documentation rides the next release).
packaging/**
scripts/**
share/**
Dockerfile
console/**
images.lock
bench/vs.py
bench/llm_load.py
bench/energy.sh
bench/agent_trace.py
bench/agent_trace_gen.py
bench/apb/apb.py
bench/apb/capacity.py
bench/competitors.lock
oracle/bundle.py
oracle/project.py
oracle/validate.py
oracle/share.py
oracle/schema/bundle-v1.json
